mb|1C|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North should open 1@C. It clearly meets the requirements for both standard |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| and if you deduct one point for the @DQx doubleton using  Bergen ^*BAdjusted Points^*n.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 1 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Further, in general when you have a 5 card major and 6 card minor you try to open 1 of the minor. However when your major is hearts and you are afraid of a 1@S response (which will happen quite frequently) and your hand is not strong enough to |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=reverses,Reverses^*N|CP||FP||at| to 2@H over 1@S, which I think is true with the North hand then you should consider opening 1@H.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 2 ***** |


mb|1D|mb|1S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|2C|mb|P|mb|P|mb|P|
pg| ***** 3 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Although we are in a perfectly good club partial if I was a little stronger, we might have missed game in our 8 card heart fit.|
