mb|1H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Using straight HCP the hand meets the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| (11 HCP and 9 cards in the red suits). However, you should use Bergen ^*BAdjusted Points^*n when doing the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| calculation meaning you take into account all |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenstartingpoints,Bergen Starting Points^*N|CP||FP||at| rules except length (e.g. HCP, quality suits, dubious shortness, Aces/Tens vs. Queens/Jacks).|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow a link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 19 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In that case you would deduct one for singleton @SK and the hand would not meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule Of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| although, it is fine to open. I am just making an observation.|
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BMovie Maker: ^*NHumbly, I would like to propose to add ^*BHONDO RULE OF 20^*n to American bridge Science. It is similar to standard |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=ruleof20,Rule of 20^*N|CP||FP||at| except you need to use Bergen ^*BAdjusted Points^*n in the calculation.All in favor please say Aye.|
PG| ***** 21 ***** |


mb|P|mb|2H|mb|D|mb|P|mb|2S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|P|mb|P|mb|3H|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I like the 3@H bid. It meets my competitive guidelines. If the points are evenly distributed (which they are on this board) and they are in an 8 card fit at the 2 level, even though your side only has 8 hearts, it is okay to bid 3 over 2 and violate the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| in this situation. |
PG| ***** 22 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Because if you let them play at the 2 level, you are very likely getting at best an average result and often a below average result. So you should generally try to avoid having them play at the 2 level in an 8 card fit.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BA Kib: ^*NOnly with favorable vulnerability?|
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|No. Always.|
PG| ***** 25 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Similarly you should not bid "3 over 3" unless you have a 9 card fit (meaning you meet the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at|) or you have a singleton.|
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


