mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3D|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|The 3@D bid is a game try, asking East whether or not they have more than a minimum limit raise (good 11 or 12) or a diamond card and and at least 11.|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


mb|P|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4S|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|East has 11 HCP, plus 1 point for the quality suit, and the @DA, therefore, has a clear bid of 4@S. |
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Now let's go back to the West bid. Marty Bergen has a good rule which I usually follow. That is, if partner makes a limit raise and I have a singleton or void I always bid game regardless of hand strength. So using that rule West could have bid 4@S right away, though, 3@D was reasonable also.|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


